WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.110
- Welcome back.

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:02.910
As we close our Veteran's Day show,

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:04.440
I have one more story to share.

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:05.673
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:10.980
David and Sylvia were
high school sweethearts

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:12.270
from Philadelphia.

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:14.240
In the wake of Pearl
Harbor, David enlisted

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:16.140
and was sent overseas.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:19.680
He fought the Nazi army through
North Africa, Italy, France

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:21.270
and finally Germany.

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:23.130
Then he deployed to the Pacific Theater

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:25.440
for the final months of the war.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:27.739
Meanwhile, Sylvia did her
part at the Philadelphia

00:00:27.739 --> 00:00:31.350
Navy Yard helping build
ships for the war effort.

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:32.730
Everybody doing their part.

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:35.160
Before David returned home,
he wrote his sister to

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:36.570
buy a ring for Sylvia.

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:37.710
Come on now.

00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:40.680
Sylvia agreed to marry
him and just 10 days

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:43.560
after he arrived home,
they exchanged vows.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:47.407
76 years later,

00:00:47.407 --> 00:00:50.100
they're still going strong.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:52.320
Say hello to David and Sylvia

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:54.363
watching on NBC Fort Washington at two.

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:57.453
- [Kelly] Hello.

00:01:01.097 --> 00:01:01.930
Hello, David.

00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:03.390
Hello, Sylvia.

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:07.170
First, I just wanna say thank
you so much to both of you

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:09.030
your incredible service to this country.

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:10.773
Thank you, Thank you, thank you.

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:15.300
And David, you didn't waste any time.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:18.633
So why was it so important to
get married when you got back?

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:22.000
- Well, you know, I was away

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:24.430
for four years

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:26.670
and, uh

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:30.460
made it okay, which there was some doubt

00:01:31.445 --> 00:01:35.523
with everything that I
saw in both theaters.

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:39.210
Anyway,

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:42.660
I wanted to get out of the service.

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:44.373
I've been in long enough.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:48.360
And start a family.

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:50.050
So that's basically, you know

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:54.540
you know how I felt about the whole thing.

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:57.000
- [Kelly] Yeah. So,
Sylvia, what's the secret

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:58.380
to a long marriage like yours?

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:01.080
I don't even know anybody that's
been married for 76 years.

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:02.580
Congratulations.

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:03.870
- Just live your life.

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:06.300
You respect each other and you go along

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.670
and have your wonderful family

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:11.400
and all your grandkids and so forth

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:14.490
and you don't even realize
that the time is going by.

00:02:14.490 --> 00:02:15.870
And here we are.

00:02:15.870 --> 00:02:17.883
- [David] I just wanna add one thing.

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:20.318
Respect.

00:02:20.318 --> 00:02:21.151
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:21.151 --> 00:02:23.130
- That was the biggest thing.

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:26.010
You must respect one another

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:30.990
for as many years as you're
together and beyond that.

00:02:30.990 --> 00:02:32.850
- Yeah. Finding a partner like that,

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:35.160
that's beautiful you guys.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:37.650
Well, David, what do you
want people to remember

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:39.450
this Veteran's Day?

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:42.240
- I want them think about,

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:45.840
there's so many wonderful people that

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:50.373
lost their lives during the war.

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:56.160
I lost many, many very close buddies.

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:59.700
I just want there to be peace.

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:02.190
People should respect each other.

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:04.050
No more wars.

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:07.110
I know that's difficult to to say,

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:08.790
but this is it.

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:12.430
We don't need wars to
settle our differences.

00:03:12.430 --> 00:03:15.420
- [Kelly] Amen. I'm with you, man.

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:17.370
Well, thank you so much, David.

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:19.590
Thank you, Sylvia, for taking the time.

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:21.210
I know you're not on social media,

00:03:21.210 --> 00:03:24.150
but I'm still liking your
post right now, anyway.

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:25.620
And that's not all.

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:28.350
Our season long Partner
Pilot Pin makers of G2,

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:30.060
the go-to pen of the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:31.920
want to honor people like you,

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:34.140
who have given so much to this country.

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:37.263
So they're gonna be writing
you a check for $1,000.

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:43.740
That's David, that,

00:03:43.740 --> 00:03:46.950
that is the second nudge
I've seen from Sylvia.

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:47.783
That was amazing.

00:03:47.783 --> 00:03:49.350
That's the second nudge.

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:51.153
You gotta take her out on a date.

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:54.960
Thank you guys so much.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:57.570
Y'all have a blessed day.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.520
Thank you to all our guests this hour.

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:03.665
Jonathan Majors, Hospital
Corpsman, Tarika Harris, Sammy,

00:04:03.665 --> 00:04:06.960
Greg Morgan, Staff
Sergeant Shaquel McKenna

00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:08.550
and specialist Kevin Ortiz.

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:10.200
Y'all have a great day, and if it's not,

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:11.203
try and change it.

